            id: "fastapi-vs-django",
            q: "FastAPI or Django: when do you choose which?",
            wants: "Whether you pick a tool for the job and understand each framework's strengths.",
            answer: "Django is 'batteries included': ORM, migrations, admin, authentication, forms; it fits monoliths, CRUD services and projects that need an admin panel from day one (for APIs people usually add Django REST Framework). FastAPI is a lightweight ASGI framework for APIs: validation via Pydantic based on type hints, automatic OpenAPI/Swagger docs and native async support. It is a common choice for microservices, I/O-heavy services and serving ML models; the ORM, migrations and admin have to be chosen separately (for example SQLAlchemy + Alembic).",
            source: { title: "FastAPI docs: Alternatives, Inspiration and Comparisons", url: "https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/alternatives/" },
